card.statement:
Let $\ff$ be a field of characteristic different from 2 with nonidentity involution. Let $V$ be a vector space over $\ff$ with nondegenerate diagonalizable sesquilinear form $\mc F:V\times V\to\ff$. Let $\mc A:V\to V$ be an isometric (respectively, $\zeta $-adjoint with $\zeta \in\{1,-1\}$) linear operator. Then

\begin{equation}
(\mc A,\mc F)_V=(\mc A_1,e_1\mc F_1)_{V_1}\oplus\dots\oplus (\mc A_t,e_t\mc F_t)_{V_t},\quad e_1,\dots,e_t\in r(\ffff),
\end{equation}

in which all $e_1,\dots,e_t$ are distinct and each $\mc A_i$ is an isometric (respectively, $\zeta  $-adjoint) linear operator on a vector space $V_i$ over $\ff$ with a nondegenerate Hermitian form $\mc F_i:V_i\times V_i\to\ff$. The summands in <<ref:rmr>> are uniquely determined by $(\mc A,\mc F)_V$, up to permutations and replacements of all $(\mc A_i,\mc F_i)_{V_i}$ by isomorphic pairs.
